# Regression key script for inc-7ml0: TextTerm::ReadLine wrote every typed
# character into `char Input[160]` (inc/Term.h:326) with no bound on the
# index (`Input[loc++] = (char)ch`, src/Term.cpp:3277), so the 161st
# character -- and the Enter key's terminating NUL right after it -- land
# outside the buffer.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_LOAD=tools/fixtures/chars/orc-barbarian-seed1-opt0822.sav \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/readline-overflow.keys 1
#
# WHY THE CHARACTER SHEET'S FILENAME PROMPT, NOT KY_CMD_JOURNAL. The bead
# names KY_CMD_JOURNAL (Ctrl+E) as an ordinary-play caller, but Ctrl+E only
# dispatches under RoguelikeKeySet (src/Tables.cpp:4849) -- StandardKeySet has
# no JOURNAL binding at all (src/Wposix.cpp:1604 picks the keyset from
# OPT_ROGUELIKE), so a fixture built under this project's usual settings never
# reaches it. TextTerm::DisplayCharSheet's own loop reads with
# GetCharCmd(KY_CMD_ARROW_MODE) (src/Managers.cpp:2284), which -- see the
# `mode == KY_CMD_ARROW_MODE` guard in posixTerm::GetCharCmd
# (src/Wposix.cpp:1699-1701) -- returns every non-arrow key raw, keyset and
# options irrelevant. Its [W]rite Dump case (src/Managers.cpp:2500-2509) calls
# the same ReadLine, with no StringPrompt in between, and needs no wizard mode
# either: [D] Display Character reaches it from ordinary play
# (src/Player.cpp:833, KY_CMD_CHAR_SHEET).
#
# Types 161 lowercase 'x' -- one more than Input can hold -- as the dump
# filename, so the stored (and possibly overflowed) text becomes a file name
# under logs/ that tools/check_readline_overflow.sh can measure directly by
# its length, with no probe and no screen-width truncation to allow for. Then
# does it again with a short, ordinary name, to prove the prompt is still
# usable afterward.
#
# 161 is deliberate, not a round number: it is the smallest overflow that
# still proves the defect, so the corruption this run can cause (if the fix
# is absent) stays inside the two bytes right after Input -- int8 linepos and
# int8 linenum (inc/Term.h:327) -- and nowhere near WViewList's Thing*
# pointer six bytes further on.

@dump:arrival

s                       # one real turn, so this counts as a session
@dump:played

d                       # KY_CMD_CHAR_SHEET: Display Character
@expect "[W]rite Dump"
@dump:sheet

w                       # [W]rite Dump -- "Filename:"
@dump:filename-prompt
"xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"
ENTER
@dump:overflow-dumped

w                       # the prompt must still work for an ordinary name
"stillusable"
ENTER
@dump:second-dumped

ESC                     # leave the sheet, back to play mode
@dump:back-in-play
